  {
    "id": "7734ee1f2ab748ce0434",
    "source": "Lay an SRD disease ({0}), a madness or a poison on a character; the server rolls the save and holds the effects from then on. A disease is a CON save against catching it, symptoms after their incubation, then the disease's own saves after each long rest; lesser restoration cures it. For a madness, pass its duration (short, long or indefinite); the server rolls that table and how long it lasts, and applies the conditions; pass saveDc (and saveAbility wis or cha) for an effect that allows a save. The SRD poisons are {1}, and the injury poisons when a poisoned blade strikes a character; the server rolls the CON save, the damage and the conditions. The table's own diseases and poisons from the workshop are named under GAME STATE and work the same way. Never narrate a disease, madness or poison taking hold without this call.",
    "sourceHash": "7734ee1f2ab748ce043479a0c99299122bb59191617c36dcf369b6456e6c0f10",
